# Background theory for the BCP 47 slice: registry uniqueness
#
# RFC 5646 section 2.2.1 states that every primary language subtag identifies
# a distinct language.  The parties adopt this as a rule, and it generates
# pairwise distinctness over the fifteen subtags of the slice.
#
# Distinctness, not disjointness.  Distinctness denies that two concepts are
# interpreted as the same element; disjointness denies that anything lies
# below both.  A registry publishes no order, so only distinctness is
# available and only distinctness is needed.
#
# A party may withdraw this rule.  Doing so reopens any Incompatible verdict
# that rested on it, without disputing the registry itself.

@prefix odrlkb:  <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/bcp47#> .
@prefix bt:      <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/background#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/bcp47/uniqueness> a bt:BackgroundTheory ;
    dcterms:title "Registry uniqueness for BCP 47 primary subtags"@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5646#section-2.2.1> ;
    bt:generatedBy bt:PairwiseDistinctness ;
    bt:appliesTo <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/bcp47> .

[] a owl:AllDifferent ;
    owl:distinctMembers (
        odrlkb:bg odrlkb:cs odrlkb:da odrlkb:de odrlkb:el
        odrlkb:en odrlkb:es odrlkb:fi odrlkb:fr odrlkb:hu
        odrlkb:it odrlkb:nl odrlkb:pl odrlkb:pt odrlkb:sv
    ) .
